# Autonomous Software Development Agreement

This draft agreement governs the development and delivery of a decentralized computing engine under the **Blockchain Markdown (.bmd)** protocol.

<!-- bmd:insert_co_sign_button label="Accept and Co-Sign as Client" -->

---

## 1. Scope of Work

The Emitter shall engineer, test, and package the core modules according to deterministic cryptographic standards. The recipient shall review the code upon delivery.

## 2. Milestone Deliverables and Compensation

| Milestone | Deliverable Description | Allocation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Phase 1: Architecture** | Cryptographic engine specification and memory model | 25% |
| **Phase 2: Core Engine** | C11 high-assurance implementation with Ed25519 signatures | 45% |
| **Phase 3: Studio & Agent** | Desktop Mini-IDE interface and autonomous document generator | 30% |

## 3. Intellectual Property and Final Sealing

Upon final co-signature, editing privileges are permanently frozen. The emitter's private key seals the block into the SHA-512 custody ledger.
